-- ============================================================
-- Car families: full catalog backfill.
--
-- Generated by server/tools/car_families/build_families.py from
-- server/tools/car_families/mapping.csv. That script's docstring documents
-- the grouping algorithm (token-prefix match, then variant-suffix reduction
-- shared by >= 2 models); server/tools/car_families/overrides.csv is the
-- explicit, human-reviewed list of every exception the algorithm can't
-- resolve on its own (aliases joined by "/", electric variants that should
-- still share the combustion model's family, brand-specific spelling quirks,
-- etc). Regenerate this file from those sources rather than hand-editing it.
--
-- Part 1 - explicit multi-model families (e.g. every Golf variant under
--          "Volkswagen Golf"): one INSERT for every family, then one UPDATE
--          per family that links exactly its enumerated members. No LIKE or
--          other prefix/substring matching.
-- Part 2 - singleton sweep: any car_models row still without a family_id
--          after part 1 gets its own singleton family named after itself.
--          Guarantees family_id IS NOT NULL for every row, including any
--          model added to the catalog later.
--
-- Idempotent: every INSERT uses ON CONFLICT DO NOTHING, every UPDATE is
-- filtered by WHERE, and part 2 only touches rows still unassigned.
-- ============================================================

